  "id": "COMPOUND:24239 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 2',4'-Dimethoxy-3'-methylpropiophenone may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C (PDE6C). This compound is implicated in multiple pathways, with its target being Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is further targeted by several other molecules, including 6-C-Methylquercetin 3-methyl ether and 14,15,16-Trimethoxy-10-methyl-10-azatetracyclo[7.7.1.02,7.013,17]heptadeca-1(17),2,4,6,8,13,15-heptaene-11,12-dione. These targets are all involved in signaling pathways that regulate PDE6C activity, suggesting a possible role for 2',4'-Dimethoxy-3'-methylpropiophenone in modulating PDE6C function. The evidence is supported by multiple high-scoring paths, indicating a consistent and plausible mechanistic link. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential to influence PDE6C through a series of intermediate targets, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
